    "correctRationale": "Bigtable stores rows sorted lexicographically by row key and reads efficiently by prefix scan over a contiguous range. The query is: one vehicle, one event type, a time interval. A key of vehicleID#eventID#timestamp places exactly those rows next to each other, so the query becomes a single narrow range scan. It also avoids hotspotting, because vehicle IDs distribute writes across the key space instead of concentrating them.",
