    "correctRationale": "The requirement is not about connectivity but about insulating dependent applications from a backend that will change shape. Apigee sits in front as an API facade: today its proxies route to the migrated monolith, and as pieces are carved into microservices the routing and transformation policies are updated inside Apigee so each consumer keeps calling the same unchanged contract. That confines the modernization blast radius to the facade configuration instead of every dependent application.",
