    "difficulty": 3,
    "question": "You have a Compute Engine application that you want to autoscale when total memory usage exceeds 80%. You have installed the Cloud Monitoring agent and configured the autoscaling policy as shown above. You observe that the application does not scale under high load. You want to resolve this. What should you do?",
    "images": [
      {
        "url": "/question-images/gcp-pca/q199-memory-metric-autoscaling.png",
        "alt": "Autoscaling policy: metric agent.googleapis.com/memory/percent_used, filter chaining metric.label.state = 'used' AND 'buffered' AND 'cached' AND 'slab', target utilization 80, target type GAUGE"
      }
    ],
    "options": [
      "A. Change the Target type to DELTA_PER_MINUTE.",
      "B. Change the Metric identifier to agent.googleapis.com/memory/bytes_used.",
      "C. Change the filter to metric.label.state = 'used'.",
      "D. Change the filter to metric.label.state = 'free' and the Target utilization to 20."
    ],
    "correct": 2,
    "explanation": "A time series carries exactly one state label, so a filter requiring 'used' AND 'buffered' AND 'cached' AND 'slab' simultaneously matches nothing. Filtering on a single state fixes it.",
