    "correctRationale": "Google Cloud validates the entire address space when you establish VPC Network Peering and refuses the connection if any subnet ranges collide, regardless of which subnets you actually intend to use. Cloud VPN has no such restriction because reachability is determined by the routes you advertise: you configure BGP or static routes to carry only the specific non-overlapping ranges where the applications live, leaving the conflicting ranges unadvertised. That delivers private connectivity without renumbering anything.",
