    "correctRationale": "A regional SSD persistent disk writes every block synchronously to replicas in two zones of the region, so at the moment a zone fails the surviving replica holds every acknowledged write and data loss is zero. Force-attach lets the standby instance in the other zone take the disk immediately without waiting for the failed instance, which keeps downtime to the time it takes to attach and start the application. Being SSD-backed, it also satisfies the high performance requirement.",
