    "discussionSummary": "Consensus C: Binary Authorization enforces that only attested images run, which is the managed Google Cloud answer to this promotion-gate problem.",
    "conceptSummary": "Enforcing environment promotion order with Binary Authorization attestations.",
    "correctRationale": "Binary Authorization is an admission controller built into GKE. You define a policy per cluster stating which attestors must have signed an image, and the CI pipeline creates an attestation when the image passes each environment. The production cluster's policy then requires the development and staging attestations, so an image that skipped them is rejected at admission. The team keeps full autonomy to deploy, and the gate is enforced by a managed feature with no code to write.",
