    "discussionSummary": "Consensus D: Cloud Functions cost nothing when idle and Firestore needs no provisioned instance, whereas Cloud SQL, GKE and Spanner all bill continuously.",
    "conceptSummary": "Cost-effective serverless architecture for low but spiky traffic.",
    "correctRationale": "With little steady traffic, the dominant cost is anything that runs continuously. Cloud Storage holds the static content for cents, Cloud Functions bill only per invocation and scale to zero between spikes, and Firestore charges per operation with no instance to provision. All three integrate with Cloud Load Balancing, through a backend bucket for the static content and a serverless network endpoint group for the functions, satisfying the load balancing requirement.",
