    "discussionSummary": "Consensus B, with the caveat that the question predates Cloud Scheduler, which is the managed cron service you would use today. The decoupling pattern through Pub/Sub is unchanged.",
    "conceptSummary": "Decoupling scheduled triggers from workers with a message queue.",
    "correctRationale": "Reliability here means a scheduled task must not be lost when the workers are unavailable. Publishing the trigger to a Pub/Sub topic stores the message durably and redelivers it until a subscriber acknowledges it, so instances that are down, restarting or saturated simply process the backlog when they recover. Calling the workers directly ties the schedule's success to their availability at that exact moment. Note the question predates Cloud Scheduler, which is the managed cron service today; the pattern is identical.",
