    "conceptSummary": "Custom cache keys to raise the Cloud CDN hit ratio.",
    "correctRationale": "Cloud CDN builds its cache key from the whole request URL, which includes the protocol. That means an identical object requested over HTTP and over HTTPS occupies two separate cache entries, so each is filled independently and each miss costs an origin fetch. Removing the protocol from the cache key collapses them into one entry, immediately improving the hit ratio without changing the content.",
