    "discussionSummary": "Consensus D: BigQuery is the OLAP warehouse, Spanner and Cloud SQL are OLTP, and Cloud SQL cannot reach hundreds of terabytes.",
    "conceptSummary": "Choosing an analytical warehouse rather than a transactional database.",
    "correctRationale": "The word OLAP means large scans and aggregations rather than small transactional reads and writes, and hundreds of terabytes rules out anything with a fixed storage ceiling. BigQuery is a serverless columnar data warehouse queried with standard SQL, designed for exactly this: scanning enormous tabular datasets for analytics and reporting with no capacity to provision.",
