    "conflict": false,
    "discussionSummary": "Consensus A: a batch call incurs the service call overhead only once, and lookup by key is cheaper than a query.",
    "conceptSummary": "Key lookups and batching in Datastore.",
    "correctRationale": "Because you already hold the identifiers, you can construct keys and read the entities directly, which bypasses index scanning entirely and is the cheapest read Datastore offers. Batching those lookups into a single get means one round trip and one service call rather than one per entity, so both the query overhead and the network overhead are minimized.",
