    "conceptSummary": "Tier-to-tier segmentation with tag-based firewall rules.",
    "correctRationale": "Instances in the same VPC can reach each other by default, so restricting the flow requires firewall rules. Tagging each tier and writing rules such as allow ingress to the api tag only from the web tag, and to the db tag only from the api tag, expresses the intended path directly and implicitly denies web to database traffic. Because tags come from the instance template, each tier remains correctly governed as it scales independently.",
