    "correctRationale": "The database crashing is one problem; the replica silently failing to be promoted is the one the question asks about. A recovery mechanism that is never exercised is effectively unverified, and the first time you learn it is broken should not be during an outage. Scheduling regular failovers turns that path into a routine, observed operation, surfacing configuration and permission problems while there is time to fix them and building operator familiarity.",
